# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever platform they are checked out on. A deploy.sh
# with CRLF fails on the first line with "syntax error near unexpected token", which reads as a
# broken script rather than as a line-ending problem — and it is checked out on Windows far
# more often than it is written there.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Bicep and JSON templates are read by Azure, not by a shell, but keeping them LF avoids noisy
# whole-file diffs when someone edits on a different platform.
*.bicep text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

*.py text
*.md text
*.js text
*.css text
*.html text
